WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.692
Can one country exit the

2
00:00:01.692 --> 00:00:03.495
Indus Waters Treaty by itself?

3
00:00:03.839 --> 00:00:05.793
Signed in 1960, it gives

4
00:00:05.793 --> 00:00:07.829
India the eastern rivers:

5
00:00:08.303 --> 00:00:10.782
the Sutlej, the Beas and the Ravi.

6
00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:12.807
Pakistan, the western rivers:

7
00:00:13.399 --> 00:00:15.203
the Indus, the Jhelum and

8
00:00:15.203 --> 00:00:15.997
the Chenab.

9
00:00:16.456 --> 00:00:18.233
Under Article XII, it can

10
00:00:18.233 --> 00:00:19.584
be changed or ended

11
00:00:20.021 --> 00:00:22.227
only by a new treaty, ratified

12
00:00:22.227 --> 00:00:23.477
for that purpose.

13
00:00:23.901 --> 00:00:26.536
On 23 April 2025, India said

14
00:00:26.536 --> 00:00:28.794
it would hold the treaty

15
00:00:28.794 --> 00:00:29.923
in abeyance,

16
00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.564
until Pakistan abjures support

17
00:00:32.564 --> 00:00:34.368
for cross-border terrorism.

18
00:00:34.729 --> 00:00:36.463
The next day, Pakistan said

19
00:00:36.463 --> 00:00:38.197
the treaty has no provision

20
00:00:38.197 --> 00:00:39.867
for unilateral suspension.

21
00:00:40.129 --> 00:00:42.683
On 31 August 2026, a Court

22
00:00:42.683 --> 00:00:45.041
of Arbitration held that

23
00:00:45.041 --> 00:00:47.791
the treaty remains in force.

24
00:00:47.983 --> 00:00:49.628
India rejected the award.

25
00:00:50.028 --> 00:00:50.794
One text.

26
00:00:51.125 --> 00:00:51.932
Two positions.

27
00:00:52.357 --> 00:00:52.911
Your turn.

28
00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.630
Which rivers go to India

29
00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:55.650
under the treaty?
